@h1 Changelog h1@

Release history for Wit. The format follows Keep a Changelog and is driven by
Changesets; pre-1.0, the version stays in the 0.x range and breaking changes are
allowed with notes.

@h2 0.1.0 — initial public release h2@

The first public release. @code wit --version code@ reports @code 0.1.0 code@.

@h3 Packages h3@

@ul
@li @strong parser strong@ — lexer and parser producing a typed AST. li@
@li @strong runtime strong@ — resolver and expander. li@
@li @strong render-html strong@ — the HTML renderer. li@
@li @strong render-markdown strong@ — the Markdown renderer. li@
@li @strong cli strong@ — the @code wit code@ command: parse, check, fmt, build,
and tour. li@
ul@

@h3 Language features h3@

@ul
@li Nodes, definitions, additive partials, records, and collections. li@
@li Data access, conditionals, iteration, and the script bridge. li@
@li The reserved core vocabulary — headings, inline marks, lists, links and media,
tables, blocks, and sectioning; see the
@a |href /docs/reference/core-vocabulary/| core vocabulary reference a@ for the
full list. li@
@li Tables in inline, schema-array, and schema-record forms. li@
@li The opaque @@@code @node code@@@ pass-through. li@
@li The form-fill body shape and record-argument invocation. li@
ul@

@h2 A note on version drift h2@

@aside(class note) 💡 The published changelog and @code wit --version code@ both
report @code 0.1.0 code@, but a @code v0.2.0 code@ git tag and later feature
commits (typed parameters, iterable captures) exist in history. The installed CLI
and the git log therefore disagree; treat @code 0.1.0 code@ as the released
version until this is reconciled. The older changelog text also cites a stale
core-vocabulary count — rely on the core vocabulary reference for the current
list, not a number. aside@

@h2 See also h2@

@a |href /docs/project/roadmap/| Roadmap a@ covers what is planned next;
@a |href /docs/start/install/| Install a@ includes the version smoke test.
